<p><strong>SCORE&nbsp;: VATSIM = 17 / 20 &nbsp;&nbsp; | &nbsp;&nbsp; IVAO = 14,5 / 20</strong><br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p data-end=\"687\" data-start=\"62\">All of this is, of course, just the opinion of your humble servant. As for me, after about twenty years on IVAO, I decided to switch to VATSIM, a choice I absolutely do not regret. I’ve noticed that IVAO has gradually declined in quality, or perhaps it’s simply that my own standards have increased over time, while VATSIM continues to see steady growth in both aircraft and controllers. The richness of the experience, the network density, and the realism of operations on VATSIM provide a particularly stimulating environment, especially for those who want to get closer to real-world piloting and air traffic control.<br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p data-end=\"1099\" data-start=\"689\">In conclusion, the most important thing is to choose the network that best suits your flying style and what you’re looking for in simulation. However, one of the great advantages of online flying is being “online” with others and sharing simulation moments together. That’s why it’s ideal, whenever possible, to operate on the same platform to facilitate group flights and foster cohesion within the airline.</p>

<p data-end=\"1391\" data-start=\"1101\">In this regard, I recommend VATSIM, which is now our reference network. That said, there’s nothing stopping you from being a member of both networks simultaneously, in fact, that’s my case, and I fully intend to keep it that way as long as IVAO continues to bring me enjoyment in flight.<br />
&nbsp;</p>

<p data-end=\"1529\" data-start=\"1393\">Whatever your choice, the key is to fully enjoy the experience and take as much pleasure in flying as we do in welcoming you among us.✈️</p>

